From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] clk: samsung: let a CMU register clocks its tables cannot
 describe

samsung_cmu_info describes a CMU's clocks as tables of standard types.
A clock with its own behaviour, such as a mux that must follow the state
of the PLL behind it, fits none of them.  An optional register_extra
callback, run by samsung_cmu_register_clocks() after the tables, lets
the SoC driver register such a clock while the CMU is still held active
and before the provider is added, so that its id resolves like the
others.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk.c | 2 ++
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.c
index 47ae261de..2d9057d52 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.c
@@ -355,6 +355,8 @@ void __init samsung_cmu_register_clocks(struct samsung_clk_provider *ctx,
 						  cmu->nr_fixed_factor_clks);
 	if (cmu->cpu_clks)
 		samsung_clk_register_cpu(ctx, cmu->cpu_clks, cmu->nr_cpu_clks);
+	if (cmu->register_extra)
+		cmu->register_extra(ctx);
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.h b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.h
index fb06caa71..f4fd271be 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.h
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk.h
@@ -365,6 +365,12 @@ struct samsung_cmu_info {
 
 	/* ARM64 Exynos CMUs */
 	bool manual_plls;
+
+	/*
+	 * Clocks that the tables above cannot describe, registered by the SoC
+	 * driver after them (optional).
+	 */
+	void (*register_extra)(struct samsung_clk_provider *ctx);
 };
 
 struct samsung_clk_provider *samsung_clk_init(struct device *dev,
-- 
